LOCATION:Ford-Crawford Hall
GEO:39.165516;-86.51774
SUMMARY:Laura Snowden\, guitar\; featuring the Bloomington Classical Guit
 ar Society – Espen Engemyr Jensen\, conductor
DESCRIPTION:Repertoire  J. S. Bach/Lévesque: Air ("On the G String")\, B
 WV 1068/iiEspen Jensen: Fugue à trois voix (1999/24)Espen Jensen: Fugue 
 à quatre voix (1999/24)Espen Jensen: Tale from the North – Of Trolls a
 nd Dragons (2022)Lisa Snowden: Black is the ColourF. Couperin/Snowden: 'L
 es Barricades Mystérieuses' from "Pièces de clavecin\, Book 2\," 1717)V
 illa-Lobos: Selections from "Five Preludes" (1940)  Lisa Snowden: This Ch
 anging Sky (2020)Chopin/Tárrega: Nocturne in E-Flat Major\, Op. 9 No. 2 
 (1830-31)Laura Snowden: CarrickfergusLaura Snowden: The Parting GlassLaur
 a Snowden: The Escape  Laura Snowden: Song for MariaLaura Snowden: As She
  SleepsAbout the Artists  Described by Acoustic Guitar Magazine as posses
 sing "multi-dimensional gifts\, imagination and fearless artistic sensibi
 lity\," LauraSnowden's eclectic musical output has ranged from playing gu
 itar solos on Lorne Balfe's soundtrack for Marvel film Black Widow to per
 forming Lisa Streich's guitar concerto with the BBC Symphony Orchestra. S
 nowden studied with Julian Bream\, during which time she gave two concert
 s at Wigmore Hall featuring premieres of his newest commissions. This led
  to international recognition and festival debuts across Europe and the U
 nited States as well as a concerto recording with Deutsches Symphonie-Orc
 hester Berlin. She has since gone on to forge her own creative and authen
 tic path as a guitarist\, composer\, and vocalist. Her eclectic repertoir
 e comprises classical\, folk and contemporary music\, with storytelling a
 t its heart\; her solo programs feature her fresh interpretations of clas
 sical works alongside her own evocative compositions\, unique vocalisatio
 ns\, and Celtic folk arrangements. Snowden's compositions and arrangement
 s have been recorded for Decca\, Rubicon Classics\, and BGS Records\, bro
 adcast on BBC Radio 3 and Classic FM\, and performed at venues including 
 Royal Albert Hall and Wigmore Hall. Her music has been commissioned by Bi
 rmingham Symphony Hall\, International Guitar Foundation\, and New York G
 uitar Festival. Shows with with folk her group Tir Eolas have included Ca
 mbridge Folk Festival\, Bestival\, and Shakespeare's Globe. Snowden's col
 laborations have included English film director and musician Sally Potter
 \, playing on the Puss in Boots soundtrack\, composer Josephine Stephenso
 n with soprano Héloïse Werner\, and movement director Roanna Mitchell a
 nd actor/director Gretchen Egolf. She has also created and recorded guita
 r arrangements for Noah and the Whale frontman Charlie Fink's album Cover
  My Tracks. Snowden's international concert appearances have included the
  Guitar Foundation of America\, Uppsala International Guitar Festival\, a
 nd Altamira Hong Kong International Guitar Symposium. She has given maste
 r classes at prestigious institutions in the UK and across the United Sta
 tes. Snowden studied at the Royal College of Music\, plays a guitar made 
 by Christopher Dean\, and is a D'Addario Artist.  A native of Norway\, Es
 pen Jensen moved to the United States in 1998 and earned master's and doc
 toral degrees\, as well as a diploma\, in guitar performance from the Ind
 iana University Jacobs School of Music. In his daily work\, Jensen leads 
 recruitment for the Jacobs School of Music as director of Admissions and 
 Financial Aid. He also remains an active performer and composer. As a gui
 tarist\, he has released several recordings of standard repertoire\, incl
 uding his two albums Nocturnal Variations and Elogio de la Danza y la Can
 cíon. As a composer\, he has composed works for solo guitar\, guitar ens
 emble\, and for a variety of chamber music settings. His 2015 work Second
 s for instance has been performed numerous times in Norway and in the Uni
 ted States\, both in its original setting for guitar and bassoon as well 
 as its alternate instrumentation of guitar and viola. His solo guitar wor
 ks have also been well received\, and two of them—Rondeau Triste and Fj
 ellets Drøm—were published by Songburd Music Publishing in 2021. Jense
 n's doctoral studies focused on music of Haiti\, particularly the Haitian
  genre of méringue. His work illuminated Haitian music as an important i
 ncubator of many of the musical characteristics found throughout the Cari
 bbean. In the process\, he transcribed and arranged a large number of Hai
 tian songs and compositions for solo guitar as well as for chamber ensemb
 les. Since earning his graduate degrees\, he has continued his work with 
 Haitian music and he often produces arrangements as well as original comp
 ositions based on Haitian musical elements. His work on Haitian music cul
 minated in 2020 with the release of his album Choucoune-Music of Haiti wh
 ich featured 15 solo guitar arrangements of Haitian music. The project wa
 s made possible by an artist grant from the Indiana Arts Commission.
