 <em>The Escape</em><br />  Laura Snowden: <em>Song for Maria<br /></em>La
 ura Snowden: <em>As She Sleeps<br /></em><br /><strong>About the Artists<
 /strong><br /><br />  Described by <em>Acoustic Guitar Magazine</em> as p
 ossessing "multi-dimensional gifts\, imagination and fearless artistic se
 nsibility\," <strong>Laura</strong><strong>Snowden</strong>'s eclectic mu
 sical output has ranged from playing guitar solos on Lorne Balfe's soundt
 rack for Marvel film <em>Black Widow</em> to performing Lisa Streich's gu
 itar concerto with the BBC Symphony Orchestra. Snowden studied with Julia
 n Bream\, during which time she gave two concerts at Wigmore Hall featuri
 ng premieres of his newest commissions. This led to international recogni
 tion and festival debuts across Europe and the United States as well as a
  concerto recording with Deutsches Symphonie-Orchester Berlin. She has si
 nce gone on to forge her own creative and authentic path as a guitarist\,
  composer\, and vocalist. Her eclectic repertoire comprises classical\, f
 olk and contemporary music\, with storytelling at its heart\; her solo pr
 ograms feature her fresh interpretations of classical works alongside her
  own evocative compositions\, unique vocalisations\, and Celtic folk arra
 ngements. Snowden's compositions and arrangements have been recorded for 
 Decca\, Rubicon Classics\, and BGS Records\, broadcast on BBC Radio 3 and
  Classic FM\, and performed at venues including Royal Albert Hall and Wig
 more Hall. Her music has been commissioned by Birmingham Symphony Hall\, 
 International Guitar Foundation\, and New York Guitar Festival. Shows wit
 h with folk her group Tir Eolas have included Cambridge Folk Festival\, B
 estival\, and Shakespeare's Globe. Snowden's collaborations have included
  English film director and musician Sally Potter\, playing on the <em>Pus
 s in Boots</em> soundtrack\, composer Josephine Stephenson with soprano H
 éloïse Werner\, and movement director Roanna Mitchell and actor/directo
 r Gretchen Egolf. She has also created and recorded guitar arrangements f
 or Noah and the Whale frontman Charlie Fink's album <em>Cover My Tracks</
 em>. Snowden's international concert appearances have included the Guitar
  Foundation of America\, Uppsala International Guitar Festival\, and Alta
 mira Hong Kong International Guitar Symposium. She has given master class
 es at prestigious institutions in the UK and across the United States. Sn
 owden studied at the Royal College of Music\, plays a guitar made by Chri
 stopher Dean\, and is a D'Addario Artist.<br /><br />  A native of Norway
 \, <strong>Espen Jensen</strong> moved to the United States in 1998 and e
 arned master's and doctoral degrees\, as well as a diploma\, in guitar pe
 rformance from the Indiana University Jacobs School of Music. In his dail
 y work\, Jensen leads recruitment for the Jacobs School of Music as direc
 tor of Admissions and Financial Aid. He also remains an active performer 
 and composer. As a guitarist\, he has released several recordings of stan
 dard repertoire\, including his two albums <em>Nocturnal Variations</em> 
 and <em>Elogio de la Danza y la Cancíon</em>. As a composer\, he has com
 posed works for solo guitar\, guitar ensemble\, and for a variety of cham
 ber music settings. His 2015 work <em>Seconds</em> for instance has been 
 performed numerous times in Norway and in the United States\, both in its
  original setting for guitar and bassoon as well as its alternate instrum
 entation of guitar and viola. His solo guitar works have also been well r
 eceived\, and two of them—<em>Rondeau Triste</em> and <em>Fjellets Drø
 m</em>—were published by Songburd Music Publishing in 2021. Jensen's do
 ctoral studies focused on music of Haiti\, particularly the Haitian genre
  of méringue. His work illuminated Haitian music as an important incubat
 or of many of the musical characteristics found throughout the Caribbean.
  In the process\, he transcribed and arranged a large number of Haitian s
 ongs and compositions for solo guitar as well as for chamber ensembles. S
 ince earning his graduate degrees\, he has continued his work with Haitia
 n music and he often produces arrangements as well as original compositio
 ns based on Haitian musical elements. His work on Haitian music culminate
 d in 2020 with the release of his album <em>Choucoune-Music of Haiti</em>
  which featured 15 solo guitar arrangements of Haitian music. The project
  was made possible by an artist grant from the Indiana Arts Commission.</
