X-SOURCE:IU Jacobs School of Music
DTSTART:20260630T233000Z
DTEND:20260701T013000Z
LOCATION:Auer Hall &amp\; LIVE@jacobs
SUMMARY:Gregory Sioles\, piano
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy this performance from almost anywhere in the world viaL
 IVE@jacobs!Repertoire  Clementi: Sonata in F-Sharp Minor\, Op. 25 No. 5 (
 1790)Berio: Wasserklavier (1965)Chopin: Four Mazurkas\, Op. 41 (1839)Chop
 in: Ballade No. 2 in F Major\, Op. 38 (1839)Mussorgsky: Pictures at an Ex
 hibition (1874)About the Artist  American pianist Gregory Sioles is prais
 ed for passionate\, stylish\, and insightful performances. Sioles has bee
 n the recipient of numerous honors and awards including a Fulbright Schol
 arship and an Atwater Kent Grand Prize. He has performed on three contine
 nts at such venues as the Purcell Room (London)\, Amerika Haus (Berlin)\,
  and the Shanghai Conservatory. Following his London debut\, he made solo
  appearances in Spain\, Germany\, Switzerland\, and Scotland. In Spain an
 d in London\, he served as the teaching assistant for the legendary pedag
 ogue Maria Curcio. In addition to Curcio\, he studied with György Sebők
  and Aube Tzerko. Sioles has performed throughout the United States as a 
 recitalist and soloist with orchestra\, and been a featured artist on Nat
 ional Public Radio. An avid chamber player\, he has collaborated with num
 erous artists\, including Edgar Meyer\, Barry Tuckwell\, the Guarneri Str
 ing Quartet\, and members of the Baltimore and National symphony orchestr
 as. As part of the Washington D.C. music scene for over a decade (1991-20
 03)\, he performed solo and chamber recitals in many of the city's import
 ant halls\, including the Kennedy Center\, the National Gallery\, the Phi
 llips Collection\, the Cosmos Club\, Strathmore Hall\, and the French Emb
 assy. Recent international engagements have taken him to Taiwan\, where h
 e performed in five cities including Kaohsiung and Taipei\, and to Panama
  and Costa Rica\, where he gave chamber and solo performances and taught 
 master classes. From 2019 to 2024\, Sioles taught at the Indiana Universi
 ty Jacobs School of Music. Previously\, he taught at Louisiana State Univ
 ersity\, the University of Maryland\, and Levine Music in Washington\, D.
 C. He records for Centaur Records.
